WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.900
Here's my progress on DataCamp's Intermediate Workflow Automation with n8n course.

2
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:12.400
First, I built a webhook workflow that receives a request and sends back a reply.

3
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:19.400
Next, I added an If node, so requests missing an email get an error instead.

4
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.550
Then I flattened nested order data into simple fields using dot notation.

5
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.800
I made one workflow call another with an HTTP Request: the producer-consumer pattern.

6
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:39.100
Then I checked that reply, sending success and failure down separate paths.

7
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.850
I scheduled a workflow to run every thirty minutes, with a business-hours check.

8
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.950
Finally, I connected that schedule to the consumer workflow, as a test run.

9
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:59.200
That's Chapter One: seven practice exercises done, a quarter of the way through. Still learning.
